  "title": "The mirror lemma, refereed, and the census of counts",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Proved by hand and refereed by fresh code: a knot space whose floor states are closed under flipping every point (the not-all-equal law) reads a count of n held points mod m (n >= m - 1) only when m is even and n odd, so never three held points mod 3 without a reference, and holds their count mod 4 exactly as a full adder. Exact census of 1,128 spaces (281 lattice tori up to 20 points, 847 random spaces of 8 to 14 points, genus 1 to 3): the 8-point parity torus (2,0,4) is a full adder (parity and majority of the same three held points), 13 spaces hold one; no space holds the count mod 3 or mod 4 with one held reference point. After the run: outputs of four held points depending on all four are only the weighted majority [2a+b+c+d>=3] and maj(a,b,a+c+d), and no restriction of either is a mod-3 bit.",
